s still holding its hymn book. The pages are kelp.","loot":[{"item":"custom_qa_hymn_leaf","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true},{"item":"bones","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true}],"behavior":"wander","questArc":"tide","blueprint":"quest-arcs-v1","blueprintKey":"tide:chorister3"}},{"id":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000006","data":{"kind":"monster","name":"Bell-warden of Corrow","species":"skeleton","attackType":"hammer","level":52,"hp":625,"damage":6,"attackSpeed":2.6,"roam":1,"respawn":45,"attackable":true,"hostile":true,"scale":1,"weapon":"verditeHammer","template":"skeleton","x":3822,"z":2998,"yaw":0,"maxHit":78,"attackLevel":49,"strengthLevel":49,"defenceLevel":47,"magicLevel":21,"attackBonus":17,"defenceBonuses":{"stab":22,"slash":20,"crush":7,"magic":17,"ranged":22},"xpReward":1154,"goldReward":146,"shield":"verditeHeaterShield","gear":["verditeHornedHelm","verditeBreastplate","verditeGreaves","verditeSabatons"],"examine":"It guards the bell-ropes. Nobody told it they were cut.","loot":[{"item":"bones","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true}],"behavior":"wander","questArc":"tide","blueprint":"quest-arcs-v1","blueprintKey":"tide:warden1","tint":7311242}},{"id":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000007","data":{"kind":"monster","name":"Bell-warden of Corrow","species":"skeleton","attackType":"hammer","level":52,"hp":625,"damage":6,"attackSpeed":2.6,"roam":1,"respawn":45,"attackable":true,"hostile":true,"scale":1,"weapon":"verditeHammer","template":"skeleton","x":3826,"z":3004,"yaw":0,"maxHit":78,"attackLevel":49,"strengthLevel":49,"defenceLevel":47,"magicLevel":21,"attackBonus":17,"defenceBonuses":{"stab":22,"slash":20,"crush":7,"magic":17,"ranged":22},"xpReward":1154,"goldReward":146,"shield":"verditeHeaterShield","gear":["verditeHornedHelm","verditeBreastplate","verditeGreaves","verditeSabatons"],"examine":"It guards the bell-ropes. Nobody told it they were cut.","loot":[{"item":"bones","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true}],"behavior":"wander","questArc":"tide","blueprint":"quest-arcs-v1","blueprintKey":"tide:warden2","tint":7311242}},{"id":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000008","data":{"kind":"monster","name":"The Choirmistress Below","species":"revenant","attackType":"magic","level":88,"hp":2630,"damage":14,"attackSpeed":3.6,"roam":1,"respawn":90,"attackable":true,"hostile":true,"scale":2.1,"template":"revenant","x":3870,"z":3002,"yaw":0,"maxHit":179,"attackLevel":90,"strengthLevel":86,"defenceLevel":81,"magicLevel":95,"attackBonus":41,"defenceBonuses":{"stab":35,"slash":35,"crush":35,"magic":17,"ranged":35},"xpReward":5773,"goldReward":713,"tint":5209990,"eyes":12124146,"examine":"She rang the warning bell until the rope was cut. She has been ringing nothing ever since.","loot":[{"item":"custom_qa_corrow_bell","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true},{"item":"bones","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true}],"behavior":"wander","questArc":"tide","blueprint":"quest-arcs-v1","blueprintKey":"tide:choirmistress","aura":8380632,"crown":true}},{"id":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000009","data":{"kind":"monster","name":"The Choirmistress’s Lament","species":"revenant","attackType":"magic","level":110,"hp":4080,"damage":19,"attackSpeed":3.4,"roam":1,"respawn":300,"attackable":true,"hostile":true,"scale":2.5,"template":"revenant","x":3848,"z":3400,"yaw":0,"maxHit":241,"attackLevel":113,"strengthLevel":107,"defenceLevel":101,"magicLevel":119,"attackBonus":50,"defenceBonuses":{"stab":43,"slash":43,"crush":43,"magic":22,"ranged":43},"xpReward":8910,"goldReward":1073,"tint":3828338,"eyes":16777215,"examine":"Her grief, given a shape and a deeper room. Harder mode.","loot":[{"item":"rawStormfin","min":2,"max":5,"chance":1,"always":true},{"item":"silverBar","min":2,"max":6,"chance":0.5},{"item":"cutGem","min":1,"max":3,"chance":0.5},{"item":"bones","min":1,"max":1,"chance":1,"always":true}],"behavior":"wander","questArc":"tide","blueprint":"quest-arcs-v1","blueprintKey":"tide:lament","aura":6281448,"crown":true}}]$j$::jsonb);

-- Quests (validated by quest_v2_check; edit them later in the Game console › Quests).
select eldervale_private.quest_arc_put('a3c0b000-0004-4000-8000-000000000001',$q${"chain":"arc-tide","order":1,"published":true,"objectives":[],"key":"arc-tide-1","name":"Bells Beneath the Tide","questPoints":1,"difficulty":"Novice","length":"Short","giver":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000001","icon":"rawShrimp","description":"At low tide the nets of Saltglass come up torn, and the fishermen swear they hear bells under the bay. Harbourmaster Tidewell would like it to stop. Quietly.","dialogue":{"offer":[{"who":"npc","text":"Torn nets every low tide. My fishermen blame bells. Under the sea. Ringing."},{"who":"npc","text":"There are no bells under the sea. There is a reef, and there are idiots. Find out which is tearing my nets."},{"who":"player","text":"And if it is bells?"},{"who":"npc","text":"Then find out quietly. Bells are bad for business."}],"progress":[{"who":"npc","text":"Well? Reef or idiots?"}],"complete":[{"who":"npc","text":"Bells. Under the bay. And a child who sings a hymn nobody has sung in two hundred years."},{"who":"npc","text":"...Keep this to yourself, would you? Here. For your trouble. And your silence."}]},"stages":[{"id":"agathe","journal":"Harbourmaster Tidewell asked me to find out what tears the Saltglass nets at low tide. Agathe the Net-Mender, by the net loft, sees every torn net in the harbour.","objectives":[{"type":"talk","target":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000002","amount":1,"label":"Ask Agathe the Net-Mender about the torn nets","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"Reef? Pah. Reefs fray a net. These are cut clean, like something swung through them. Something metal."},{"who":"npc","text":"Mend me this one and catch something with it, and you will see for yourself."}]}]},{"id":"mend","journal":"Agathe says the nets are cut clean, as if by swinging metal. She will lend me a net if I help her mend it with two lengths of thread.","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000002","objectives":[{"type":"collect","target":"thread","amount":2,"label":"Bring Agathe two lengths of thread"}],"dialogue":{"advance":[{"who":"npc","text":"There. Good as new, or as good as anything is around here. Go and fish with it at low tide."}]}},{"id":"fish","journal":"Agathe mended the net. I should fish at Saltglass and see what comes up.","objectives":[{"type":"event","event":"fishing","amount":3,"label":"Fish in Saltglass Bay with Agathe’s net"}]},{"id":"listen","journal":"Every catch came up with weed wrapped round a scrap of old bell-rope. At dusk the fishermen listen along the western shore. I should listen where the shore bends: at the cove, the point and the long strand.","onEnter":{"cutscene":"bells"},"objectives":[{"type":"visit","x":284,"z":370,"radius":4,"amount":1,"label":"Listen at the cove by the landing"},{"type":"visit","x":262,"z":375,"radius":4,"amount":1,"label":"Listen at the point"},{"type":"visit","x":240,"z":383,"radius":4,"amount":1,"label":"Listen along the long strand"}]},{"id":"tobin","journal":"I heard them: bells, far out and deep, ringing a tune I almost knew. A small boy called Tobin was humming the same tune on the landing.","objectives":[{"type":"talk","target":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000003","amount":1,"label":"Ask Little Tobin about the tune","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"It is the bell song. I sing it in my sleep. Mum says I never learned it anywhere."},{"who":"npc","text":"The bells are sad. They have been ringing for ages and nobody comes."}]}]}],"cutscenes":{"bells":{"name":"Bells under the bay","steps":[{"fade":"in","ms":700,"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000003","distance":5,"height":2.2,"angle":30}},{"title":"Bells under the bay","subtitle":"Saltglass Landing, at dusk","ms":2400},{"say":{"who":"npc","name":"Little Tobin","text":"There! Can you hear it? Under the water. Ding. Ding. Ding-dong. It is a song."},"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000003","distance":3.4,"height":1.8,"angle":35}},{"fade":"out","ms":600}]},"quiet":{"name":"Quietly","steps":[{"fade":"in","ms":700,"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000001","distance":5,"height":2.2,"angle":30}},{"title":"A quiet word","subtitle":"Saltglass harbour","ms":2400},{"say":{"who":"npc","name":"Harbourmaster Corwen Tidewell","text":"Bells. Children singing dead hymns. If this gets out, nobody will fish here for a year. Quietly, I said."},"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000001","distance":3.4,"height":1.8,"angle":35}},{"fade":"out","ms":600}]}},"onComplete":{"cutscene":"quiet"},"journalDone":"The Saltglass nets are cut by swinging bells far under the bay; I heard them at dusk from the western shore. Little Tobin hums their tune in his sleep, though he never learned it. Harbourmaster Tidewell wants it kept quiet.","gold":150,"xp":{"fishing":1500,"crafting":1000},"lamps":[{"perLevel":10,"minLevel":5,"label":"Low-tide lamp"}],"unlocks":[{"type":"flag","id":"tide.bells_heard","label":"Saltglass has heard the bells"},{"type":"dialogue","id":"dialogue.tide-agathe-1","label":"Agathe saves the rope","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000002","lines":[{"who":"npc","text":"I keep every scrap of bell-rope that comes up now. There is a lot of it. Somebody cut a great many ropes, a long time ago."}]}]}$q$::jsonb);
select eldervale_private.quest_arc_put('a3c0b000-0004-4000-8000-000000000002',$q${"chain":"arc-tide","order":2,"published":true,"objectives":[],"key":"arc-tide-2","name":"The Fen Witch’s Price","questPoints":2,"difficulty":"Intermediate","length":"Medium","giver":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","icon":"rawTrout","requirements":{"quests":["arc-tide-1"],"skills":{"fishing":{"level":25,"boostable":false},"herblore":{"level":10,"boostable":false}}},"description":"Scholar Ilse Quillon has heard about the bells. The only person alive who might remember the drowning of Old Corrow is Grandmother Moss, who lives in the fens on the far side of Eldervale and charges for everything.","dialogue":{"offer":[{"who":"npc","text":"Bells under the bay! Old Corrow! I have waited my whole life for someone to say those words to me."},{"who":"npc","text":"Corrow drowned two hundred years ago. Every record calls it a storm. Grandmother Moss, in the fens, calls it something else, and she is older than the records."},{"who":"npc","text":"She charges for answers. Pay her, whatever it is. Within reason. Within most reasons."}],"progress":[{"who":"npc","text":"Did Moss talk? Did she charge you a tooth? She charged me a tooth."}],"complete":[{"who":"npc","text":"A bargain with the tide. A town that sang for its fish, and a warning bell that rang for nobody."},{"who":"npc","text":"And Reedly will run the old Mirewater ferry for you? Between the fens and the bay? That has not run since my grandmother was a girl. Wonderful."}]},"branchDialogue":[{"stage":"complete","ifFlags":{"moss_charm":true},"lines":[{"who":"npc","text":"You took Moss’s charm. I can smell it from here. Peat and pondweed and something older."},{"who":"npc","text":"Still, she told you the bargain, and Reedly will run the Mirewater ferry for you. Wonderful."}]}],"stages":[{"id":"moss","journal":"Scholar Ilse Quillon sent me across Eldervale to the fens in the south-west, to ask Grandmother Moss about the drowning of Old Corrow.","objectives":[{"type":"talk","target":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","amount":1,"label":"Find Grandmother Moss in the fens","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"Corrow? Ha! Two hundred years and somebody finally asks properly."},{"who":"npc","text":"Answers cost. First, my eel-traps. Two little thieves have been at them. Wearing my eels. Wearing them."}]}]},{"id":"eels","journal":"Grandmother Moss will talk about Corrow, for a price. First, two bog eel-thieves have been robbing her traps.","objectives":[{"type":"event","event":"death","targets":["a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000001","a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000002"],"amount":2,"label":"Deal with the bog eel-thieves"}]},{"id":"supper","journal":"The eel-thieves are gone. Moss wants a proper supper of three raw trout before she will tell me anything. She does her own cooking. “Nobody else does it right.”","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","objectives":[{"type":"collect","target":"rawTrout","amount":3,"label":"Bring Grandmother Moss three raw trout"}],"dialogue":{"choice":[{"who":"npc","text":"Corrow sang to the tide. Every year, a hymn, and the tide filled their nets. A bargain. Then one year the warning bell rang, the storm came in, and nobody climbed the hill."},{"who":"npc","text":"Somebody had cut the bell-ropes, see. Nobody heard the warning. The choir sang all the way down."},{"who":"npc","text":"Now. I can give you a charm that lets you hear what the drowned hear. It will cost you a little of your sleep. Or you can go with what you have."}]},"choices":[{"id":"charm","label":"Take Moss’s charm and hear what the drowned hear.","flags":{"moss_charm":true},"dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"Clever. Wear it on your ear and keep a candle by your bed. You will dream in hymns."}]},{"id":"refuse","label":"Thank her, and keep your sleep.","flags":{"refused_charm":true},"dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"Sensible. Boring, but sensible. Off you go."}]}]},{"id":"ferry","journal":"Moss told me the truth of Corrow: the town sang to the tide for its catch, and drowned when someone cut the warning bell’s ropes. Ferryman Reedly, at the fen landing nearby, is the last who knows the old Mirewater channels to the bay.","objectives":[{"type":"talk","target":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000005","amount":1,"label":"Ask Ferryman Reedly about the Mirewater channels","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"The Mirewater! Fens to the bay, under the old willows and out by the drowned dyke. Nobody has asked for it in forty years."},{"who":"npc","text":"For a friend of Moss? I will run it whenever you ring for me."}]}]}],"cutscenes":{"fens":{"name":"The fen witch","steps":[{"fade":"in","ms":700,"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","distance":5,"height":2.2,"angle":30}},{"title":"The fens","subtitle":"South-west Eldervale","ms":2400},{"say":{"who":"npc","name":"Grandmother Moss","text":"Wipe your boots. No, the other way. Now sit, and do not touch the jar with the face in it."},"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","distance":3.4,"height":1.8,"angle":35}},{"fade":"out","ms":600}]},"ferry":{"name":"The Mirewater ferry","steps":[{"fade":"in","ms":700,"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000005","distance":5,"height":2.2,"angle":30}},{"title":"The Mirewater ferry","subtitle":"The fen landing","ms":2400},{"say":{"who":"npc","name":"Ferryman Ambrose Reedly","text":"Fens to the bay in an afternoon, and back by supper. Ring the landing bell and I will come."},"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000005","distance":3.4,"height":1.8,"angle":35}},{"fade":"out","ms":600}]}},"onComplete":{"cutscene":"ferry"},"journalDone":"Grandmother Moss told me Old Corrow sang a yearly hymn to the tide for its catch, and drowned when someone cut the ropes of the warning bell. Ferryman Reedly will now run the old Mirewater ferry for me between the fens and Saltglass.","journalVariants":[{"ifFlags":{"moss_charm":true},"text":"I took Moss’s charm. I dream in hymns now."},{"ifFlags":{"refused_charm":true},"text":"I refused Moss’s charm and kept my sleep."}],"gold":400,"xp":{"fishing":6000,"herblore":4000,"magic":3000},"lamps":[{"perLevel":10,"minLevel":10,"label":"Fen lamp"}],"unlocks":[{"type":"teleport","id":"teleport.ferry-fens","label":"Mirewater ferry: the fen landing","x":-176,"z":254},{"type":"teleport","id":"teleport.ferry-saltglass","label":"Mirewater ferry: Saltglass Landing","x":300,"z":350},{"type":"flag","id":"tide.corrow_bargain","label":"The Corrow bargain is remembered"},{"type":"dialogue","id":"dialogue.tide-moss-charm","label":"Moss checks on her charm","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","ifFlags":{"moss_charm":true},"lines":[{"who":"npc","text":"Still dreaming in hymns? Good. Do not sing them out loud in the fens. Things answer."}]},{"type":"dialogue","id":"dialogue.tide-reedly-2","label":"Reedly’s ferry runs","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000005","lines":[{"who":"npc","text":"The channels are deeper than I remember. Or I am shorter. One of the two."}]}]}$q$::jsonb);
select eldervale_private.quest_arc_put('a3c0b000-0004-4000-8000-000000000003',$q${"chain":"arc-tide","order":3,"published":true,"objectives":[],"key":"arc-tide-3","name":"Hymn of Salt","questPoints":2,"difficulty":"Intermediate","length":"Medium","giver":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","icon":"custom_qa_hymn_leaf","requirements":{"quests":["arc-tide-2","arc-frontier-2"],"skills":{"crafting":{"level":25,"boostable":false},"fishing":{"level":30,"boostable":false}}},"description":"If Corrow sang to the tide, its hymn can be sung again. Scholar Ilse believes the drowned choristers wandering Gloomfen still carry pages of it.","dialogue":{"offer":[{"who":"npc","text":"The drowned do not all stay drowned. Some walk the fens, carrying what they carried when the sea took them."},{"who":"npc","text":"The choristers of Corrow carried their hymn books. Pages of kelp, Moss says. Bring me three, and we can put the hymn back together."}],"progress":[{"who":"npc","text":"Three leaves. Kelp. Possibly damp. Definitely damp."}],"complete":[{"who":"npc","text":"The hymn of salt. Whole again. And shrouds for the choir, should they ever want to rest."},{"who":"npc","text":"You have done something no scholar could. Thank you."}]},"stages":[{"id":"chapel","journal":"Scholar Ilse believes the drowned choristers of Corrow wander Gloomfen carrying pages of their hymn. The old fen chapel on the edge of Gloomfen is where Moss says they gather.","objectives":[{"type":"visit","x":-246,"z":288,"radius":5,"amount":1,"label":"Find the old fen chapel in Gloomfen"}]},{"id":"choristers","journal":"Three drowned choristers circle the ruined fen chapel, singing with mouths full of water.","onEnter":{"cutscene":"choir"},"objectives":[{"type":"event","event":"death","targets":["a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000003","a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000004","a3c0a000-0004-4000-9000-000000000005"],"amount":3,"label":"Lay the drowned choristers to rest"}]},{"id":"leaves","journal":"Each chorister left a page of kelp. I should take all three hymn leaves back to Ilse at Saltglass.","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","objectives":[{"type":"collect","target":"custom_qa_hymn_leaf","amount":3,"label":"Bring Ilse three kelp hymn leaves"}],"dialogue":{"advance":[{"who":"npc","text":"Three verses, out of order, of course. One is crusted with salt. One has a bell drawn in the margin. One is smudged with the words “still water”."},{"who":"npc","text":"The hymn begins at sea and ends at rest. The bell is its heart. Put them in order for me."}]}},{"id":"order","journal":"The three verses are out of order: one crusted with salt, one with a bell in the margin, one smudged with “still water”. Ilse says the hymn begins at sea, ends at rest, and the bell is its heart.","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","objectives":[{"type":"talk","target":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","amount":1,"label":"Tell Ilse the order of the verses"}],"dialogue":{"choice":[{"who":"npc","text":"Well? Which order?"}]},"choices":[{"id":"right","label":"Salt, then bell, then still water.","flags":{"hymn_ordered":true},"next":"shrouds","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"Salt, bell, still water. Yes. Sea, heart, rest. Listen to it."}]},{"id":"bellfirst","label":"Bell, then salt, then still water.","next":"hum","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"It starts with a clang and goes nowhere. No. Ask Tobin; he sings it in his sleep."}]},{"id":"stillfirst","label":"Still water, then bell, then salt.","next":"hum","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"That is the hymn backwards, and it sounds like a curse. Ask Tobin; he sings it in his sleep."}]}]},{"id":"hum","journal":"My order was wrong. Ilse suggested I ask Little Tobin, who sings the hymn in his sleep, how it goes.","next":"order","objectives":[{"type":"talk","target":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000003","amount":1,"label":"Ask Little Tobin how the bell song goes","dialogue":[{"who":"npc","text":"It starts all salty, like the sea in your mouth. Then the bell bit, ding-dong. Then it goes quiet and calm. That is the end."}]}]},{"id":"shrouds","journal":"The hymn is whole: salt, bell, still water. Ilse asked me to bring two lengths of linen for shrouds, in case the choir ever wants to rest.","objectives":[{"type":"collect","target":"linen","amount":2,"label":"Bring Ilse two lengths of linen for shrouds"}]}],"cutscenes":{"choir":{"name":"The fen chapel","steps":[{"fade":"in","ms":700,"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","distance":5,"height":2.2,"angle":30}},{"title":"The drowned choristers","subtitle":"Gloomfen","ms":2400},{"say":{"who":"npc","name":"Grandmother Moss","text":"(Moss’s voice carries over the bog) Do not sing back to them! Whatever you do, do not sing back!"},"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004","distance":3.4,"height":1.8,"angle":35}},{"fade":"out","ms":600}]},"hymn":{"name":"The hymn of salt","steps":[{"fade":"in","ms":700,"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","distance":5,"height":2.2,"angle":30}},{"title":"The hymn of salt","subtitle":"Saltglass Landing","ms":2400},{"say":{"who":"npc","name":"Scholar Ilse Quillon","text":"Salt, bell, still water. Two hundred years, and it fits on three leaves of kelp."},"shot":{"around":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","distance":3.4,"height":1.8,"angle":35}},{"fade":"out","ms":600}]}},"onComplete":{"cutscene":"hymn"},"journalDone":"I laid three drowned choristers of Corrow to rest in Gloomfen and brought their kelp hymn leaves to Scholar Ilse. Together we put the hymn of salt back in order, and I brought linen for the choir’s shrouds.","gold":600,"xp":{"crafting":7000,"prayer":5000,"fishing":4000},"lamps":[{"perLevel":10,"minLevel":15,"label":"Hymn lamp"}],"unlocks":[{"type":"flag","id":"tide.hymn_whole","label":"The hymn of salt is whole"},{"type":"dialogue","id":"dialogue.tide-ilse-3","label":"Ilse hums the hymn","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000006","lines":[{"who":"npc","text":"I hum it while I work. The gulls have gone very quiet. I think they know it."}]},{"type":"dialogue","id":"dialogue.tide-tobin-3","label":"Tobin sleeps sound","npc":"a3c0a000-0004-4000-8000-000000000003","lines":[{"who":"npc","text":"I did not sing in my sleep last night! Mum says I snored instead. That is better. Probably."}]}]}$q$::jsonb);

commit;
